From 7097a31c3d41c31b66a9011bd601860f3dc7209d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:17:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Wire the statarb leg and fix the SIM105 so the tree seals and
 placements resume

THIS ENDS A SEVENTEEN-DAY TRADING HALT, and the interlock was never at fault.
`release.seal` raises "cannot seal a dirty tree (9 tracked code paths differ from
HEAD)", so the release identity never refreshed, `allows_new_risk` stayed false, and
the gateway refused every placement -- 1,196 `release_identity_refused` rows since
2026-09-07, one a minute, read by nobody. `MT5-SealIfClean` was healthy throughout,
16 successful seals in its own log. The rail was right and was handed a tree it could
not honestly seal.

Seven of the nine cleared as their authors committed. These two held the stat-arb
leg's registration -- `layers.py` places `statarb` in the prediction layer,
`hourly_cycle.py` adds it to discovery with an explicit 700 s budget, listed because
the 720 s default would have truncated its ~25-minute first pass at twelve minutes
every hour and left no artifact. Verified by compileall and ruff before committing:
a broken file in the tree the gateway runs would be worse than the halt.

The SIM105 was pre-existing in HEAD and had already been fixed once by another lane;
an adoption reverted that fix, which is the same class of event that reverted the
atomic `publish_frame` universe write and left the torn-parquet fault live for an hour
while `MT5-GauntletGuard` failed every five minutes unnoticed.

What the halt cost: `gold_london_am` and `gold_afternoon` were refused on the live
account for seventeen days while E8's equivalent windows placed, so the two books
diverged silently and the MT5 gold record (asia n=14, london_am n=10, afternoon n=5)
is a SELECTED sample -- the trades that got through a broken gate. The live numbers
should be expected to look worse before they look right.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZHzZoD3QX9Tx668fkAaw6
